      <!-- Rail: Five Consumer Niches Where Supply Lags -->
      <div class="rail-grid pt-2">
        <div class="rail-head space-y-3">
          <h3 class="font-serif text-lg sm:text-xl font-bold text-stone-950 dark:text-stone-50">
            Five niches where supply lags
          </h3>
          <p class="text-sm sm:text-base text-stone-700 dark:text-stone-300 leading-relaxed">
            In each of these categories, demand from middle and affluent households is growing fast, while physical supply takes years of land, trust, or engineering to add.
          </p>
        </div>

        <ul class="squares text-sm sm:text-base text-stone-800 dark:text-stone-200 leading-relaxed">
          <li>
            <strong class="text-stone-950 dark:text-stone-50">Housing:</strong> Families moving up from basic apartments want well-run communities with reliable water, power, and open spaces. Good urban land with clean titles and credible builders takes years to put together.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong class="text-stone-950 dark:text-stone-50">Travel and Leisure:</strong> India has built airports and highways faster than good places to stay. India has roughly 180,000 branded hotel rooms across the entire country, less than many single cities in Asia. Clean, mid-priced stays within driving distance of big cities remain scarce.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong class="text-stone-950 dark:text-stone-50">Clean Food:</strong> Rising incomes have come alongside high rates of diabetes and metabolic illness. More families now read labels and want clean staples. The bottleneck here is not branding or 10-minute delivery. It is farm sourcing, soil health, and cold chains that keep milk and produce clean without preservatives.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong class="text-stone-950 dark:text-stone-50">Financial Services:</strong> As households move savings from gold and fixed deposits into financial markets, they need simple tools, transparent accounting, and honest advice that does not rely on mis-selling commissions.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong class="text-stone-950 dark:text-stone-50">Cooling and Healthcare Hardware:</strong> With less than 10% AC penetration and hotter summers each year, demand for efficient cooling and airflow hardware will grow for decades. On healthcare, as parents age in nuclear families, India needs affordable diagnostics and out-of-hospital recovery care (rehab, icu-at-home, and chronic care) that frees up hospital beds.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </div>
